    "research": {
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-13",
      "reviewer": "research review",
      "searchCoverage": "Official Brevo v3 authentication (api-key header), GET /v3/account, /v3/contacts, /v3/contacts/{identifier}, /v3/contacts/folders, /v3/contacts/lists, Paris operator identity, and dated incident search (Brevo/Sendinblue + security breach/incident) reviewed on 2026-09-13. Vendor status write-up dated 2026-09-10 confirms a SAML SSO boundary flaw that granted an attacker access to 138 customer accounts (6 used to send phishing; 43 had contacts exported). Vendor claims the entry point was closed at 08:30 UTC 2026-09-10 and sessions were reset. Customer notifications (Trezor, BitBox, CoinTracking) were still publishing on 2026-09-13. This is treated as a current confirmed compromise, not a historical closed incident.",
